  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3HARRIS Technologies Integrated Systems L P obligated $1.2B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS received 166 awards with an average award size of $7.5M, and obligations fell down 22.4% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1.2B, while the Department of Homeland Security obligated $846K. Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing is the largest market for L3HARRIS with $936M in obligations. L3HARRIS also recorded obligations in Aircraft Manufacturing of $163M and Satellite Telecommunications of $72.9M. Additional reported markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) with $48.2M and Engineering Services with $11.5M. Smaller reported obligations appear in Other Support Activities for Air Transportation of $7.4M, Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing of $846K, Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing of $129K, and Hardware Manufacturing of $93.1K.",
